# NAZURI COLLECTIONS
## Technical Development Guide & Coding Standards

**Project:** Nazuri Collections Showcase Website  
**Document:** 02 – Technical Development Instructions  
**Development Environment:** Windows PC + Visual Studio Code  
**Repository:** nazuricollections-showcase  
**Primary Branch:** main  
**Status:** Initial development from a clean repository

---

# 1. Development Objective

Build the Nazuri Collections website from the beginning using a lightweight, maintainable and responsive frontend architecture.

The implementation must follow Document 01: Project Vision, Brand Strategy and Website Requirements.

All development decisions must prioritize:

- Code quality.
- Maintainability.
- Performance.
- Responsiveness.
- Accessibility.
- Security.
- Visual consistency.
- Reliable functionality.

# 2. Mandatory Technology Stack

Use the following technologies:

| Technology | Responsibility |
|---|---|
| HTML5 | Semantic page structure |
| CSS3 | Custom styling and visual design |
| Bootstrap 5 | Responsive layout and selected UI components |
| Vanilla JavaScript | Interactions and dynamic frontend functionality |
| Git | Version control |
| GitHub | Remote source code repository |

Use Bootstrap 5 and plain JavaScript.

Do not introduce React, Vue, Angular, Laravel, Django, Node.js backend frameworks or other unnecessary application frameworks.

A lightweight static frontend is the required architecture.

